<Legal
  heading="Support"
  kicker="Help"
  description="Help with Skipper — coverage, location, audio, credits, and how to reach a human."
  updated="July 15, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Skipper is a small, hand-built thing. If something's wrong, email
    <a href="mailto:hello@skipper.fm">hello@skipper.fm</a> and a human — the person who built it —
    will read it.
  </p>

  <h2>“The Skipper says he doesn't know these roads”</h2>
  <p>
    That's the honest answer, not a bug. Every story in Skipper is written and recorded for a
    specific place, and right now the only place with a finished collection is
    <strong>Lake Tahoe, California</strong>. Outside that basin there's nothing for him to tell you
    about, and he'd rather say so than make something up.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can still hear him without going anywhere: create a drive between two Tahoe points and the
    app plays the whole thing as a <strong>preview</strong> — every stop, in order, from your couch.
    More regions are the plan; there's no date to promise.
  </p>

  <h2>The stops aren't playing while I drive</h2>
  <p>A few things to check, roughly in order of likelihood:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Location permission.</strong> Skipper needs “While Using the App” to know when you've
      reached a stop. Settings → Skipper → Location.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Precise Location must be on.</strong> With it off, iOS gives a rough neighborhood
      instead of a position, and a stop can't be timed to the road.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Keep the app open.</strong> Skipper plays in the foreground while you drive — mount the
      phone, or start the drive before you set off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Thin signal.</strong> Tahoe has real dead zones. Download the drive before you leave
      and it plays from the phone with no signal at all.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Credits</h2>
  <p>
    Each account gets a set number of free drives to create. Making a drive spends one. Deleting a
    drive doesn't give it back — the work of building it already happened. <strong>Planning is
    free.</strong> Talk to the Skipper as long as you like, change your mind as often as you like,
    and throw away as many routes as you want — a credit is only spent when you tell him to build one.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    In the app: <strong>Settings → Delete account</strong>. It removes your account, your saved
    drives, and any credits you have left, straight away and for good. There's no undo, and unused
    credits don't come back. If you can't get into your account to delete it, email us.
  </p>

  <h2>Forgot your password</h2>
  <p>
    On the sign-in screen, tap <strong>“Forgot your password?”</strong> and we'll email a link. It
    works once and expires after an hour. If it doesn't turn up, check the spam bin before writing
    to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Is Skipper safe to use while driving?</h2>
  <p>
    It's built to be listened to, not looked at — start it, mount the phone, and drive. Nothing in
    Skipper needs your eyes once a drive is running. Don't handle the phone while moving; no story is
    worth it.
  </p>

  <h2>Still stuck</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:hello@skipper.fm">hello@skipper.fm</a>. Tell us what happened, roughly
    where you were, and what iPhone you're on — that's usually enough to work it out.
  </p>
  <p>
    See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
